            <div xml:id="d818">

                <pb facs="1108" n="972" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg972"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/981: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hawks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-27T15:00:00-06:00">November 27, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>152. The following telegram was sent to the Legation in Honduras: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 27, 3 p.m. With reference to your telegram of November 26, 10
                            a.m. to the Department.</p>
                        <p>The Minister for Foreign Affairs informed me today that he did not
                            consider that the Honduran reply makes it sufficiently clear that the
                            Honduran delegate will be given absolute freedom to discuss any <pb
                                facs="1109" n="973" xml:id="pg973"/> phase of the boundary question
                            and that therefore the Government of Guatemala feels that under these
                            conditions it is useless to call the conference.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hawks</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
